        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parkville%2C_Victoria",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The 2006 Commonwealth Games athlete's village was built on the former Royal Park Psychiatric Hospital site, now the residential Parkville Gardens.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        8,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parkville%2C_Victoria",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "South Parkville became Australia’s first classified metropolitan area, a status later cemented by its inclusion in the State Historic Register.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://parkvilleassociation.org.au/history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Parkville railway station, built under Grattan Street, opened in late 2025 as part of Melbourne’s Metro Rail Project.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parkville%2C_Victoria",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The University of Melbourne, erected in 1853, was the first major institution built in what is now Parkville.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
